// repro-28 — a line comment immediately before an `on mount {}` block makes the
//   whole block emit as LITERAL TEXT in the HTML instead of compiling to a
//   lifecycle hook. The on-mount loader never fires. Compile exit-0, no warning.
//
// Compiler: ../scrml @ 7c01b22a (pkg v0.7.0). Command: scrml compile repro-28.scrml -o out
//
// Expected: `on mount { @a = f() }` compiles to a mount lifecycle hook (as it does
//   with NO preceding comment).
// Actual:   the literal string `on mount { @a = f() }` appears as a text node in
//   out/repro-28.html; the hook never runs.
//
// Isolation: the trigger is specifically a `//` comment line DIRECTLY before the
//   `on mount`. A blank line in the same position does NOT trigger it; removing the
//   comment fixes it. (Bisected from giti status.scrml, where 3 on-mount loaders
//   sit under a comment and all three leak → the page is stuck on "Loading…".)
//
// giti impact: status.scrml (3 dashboard loaders never fire → page never leaves the
//   Loading skeleton in a browser).

<program>

${ function f() { return 1 } }

<a> = 0
// this comment defeats the on-mount directive on the next line
on mount { @a = f() }

<div><p>${@a}</p></div>

</program>
